<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Dostoevsky is a 43-year-old man with recurrent generalized tonic-clonic seizures, untreated for many years, and gambling disorder, who returns four weeks after his first visit and is seen by neurology today. He has had one seizure since then, about three weeks ago, at home in the early morning after writing through the night; he lives alone and woke on the floor with a bitten tongue, aching muscles, and several hours of confusion. He recalls no warning. The routine EEG two weeks ago and the epilepsy-protocol MRI were both normal. He has not gambled since the first visit. He has signed up for self-exclusion from the casinos in the state and from licensed online sites, his bank has placed a gambling block on his cards, and he has started weekly cognitive behavioral therapy with a gambling-disorder therapist. Urges are strong in the evenings, especially when money is short. A friend he trusts now co-signs any withdrawal over a set amount. He has no thoughts of suicide. He is not driving. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Seizures</td><td>One unwitnessed generalized seizure three weeks ago, after a night without sleep</td></tr><tr><td>Tests</td><td>Routine EEG and epilepsy-protocol MRI normal</td></tr><tr><td>Gambling</td><td>None since the first visit; strong evening urges</td></tr><tr><td>Safeguards</td><td>Self-exclusion, bank gambling block, co-signer for large withdrawals</td></tr><tr><td>Therapy</td><td>Weekly cognitive behavioral therapy started</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

